From: Armin <2369138+Arminova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:28:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] core lanes: burst admission, requests sent together
 start in lockstep

An idle engine holds a first arrival for TENSORFOLD_ADMIT_WAIT_MS (default 5, 0 turns it off) for requests
sent with it. When two or more wait, every one is admitted before any launches (so none takes the lone
driver) and marked a burst; a burst's prompts all fill before the next round. Identical requests then decode
in lockstep and share each round's expert work.

Same bits per stream (scheduling only): concurrent == alone 28/28 on Flash-Next. GB10, Flash-Next FP4-Local,
four identical greedy streams: code 165 -> 236 tok/s, chat 119 -> 166; mixed load unchanged.
---
 zig/src/core/lane_host.zig       | 21 +++++++++--
 zig/src/core/lane_host_admit.zig | 61 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 zig/src/core/lane_job.zig        |  1 +
 3 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

